                                          BINARY SEARCH - LEET CODE PROBLEM 35
AIM - Given a sorted array of distinct integers and a target value, return the index if the target is found. If not, return the index where it would be if it were inserted in order.                                          

ALGORITHM -Search Insert Position (Binary Search)
Start
Initialize low = 0 and high = nums.size() - 1.
Repeat while low <= high:
Calculate the middle index:
mid = low + (high - low) / 2
If nums[mid] == target:
Return mid (target found).
Else if nums[mid] < target:
Set low = mid + 1 (search in the right half).
Else:
Set high = mid - 1 (search in the left half).
If the loop ends, the target is not present.
Return low, which is the correct insertion position.
Stop

CODE: 
class Solution {
public:
    int searchInsert(vector<int>& nums, int target) {
        int low = 0;
        int high = nums.size() - 1;

        while (low <= high) {
            int mid = low + (high - low) / 2;

            if (nums[mid] == target)
                return mid;
            else if (nums[mid] < target)
                low = mid + 1;
            else
                high = mid - 1;
        }

        return low;
    }
};
